{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and lists no tracking domains.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Required-reason APIs","level":3,"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Module"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why none is a required-reason API","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileDescriptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"read","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"write","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"resize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"close","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"unlink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"createDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"setAttributes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the file protection class), ","type":"text"},{"code":"contentsOfDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"isExcludedFromBackup","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from ","type":"text"},{"code":"stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset ","type":"text"},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"FileManager.fileExists","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Data.write(to:options:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"FileVersionStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads and writes the version file’s contents, never its attributes.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sysctlbyname"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.machine"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.operatingSystemVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.infoDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale.current"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NWPathMonitor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None is on the list; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()"},{"text":" is declared as collected data below.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker’s record timestamps ("},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s inactivity is measured between records’ wall-clock timestamps, not from the system’s uptime.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Date.now","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wall-clock time, not boot time."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":", the default clock of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift